# Examples only. PowerShell does not automatically load this file.
# Set a fresh local signing secret yourself; never commit your real value.
# $env:TRIPPLANNER_SECRET_KEY = '<your-own-random-secret>'
# Optional: use your own absolute local database path for the web preview.
# $env:TRIPPLANNER_DATABASE = 'C:\your-local-folder\tripplanner.sqlite3'
# The Windows app manages its own per-profile secret and database.
# Public hosting is an EXPLICIT separate entry point: python serve_hosted.py
# Set these privately on the chosen host; this file is not automatically loaded.
# TRIPPLANNER_SECRET_KEY: your independently generated 64-character hex secret.
# TRIPPLANNER_STORAGE_DIR: existing durable mount outside the source checkout.
# TRIPPLANNER_PUBLIC_HOST: the actual DNS hostname, without https:// or a path.
# PORT: provider-supplied integer port.
# Never upload existing local/native databases. See docs/public-hosting.md.
# Selected free demo: TRIPPLANNER_STORAGE_BACKEND=postgres
# Set TRIPPLANNER_DATABASE_URL privately to the Neon URL with sslmode=verify-full.
# Do not set TRIPPLANNER_STORAGE_DIR for PostgreSQL. See docs/free-demo-hosting.md.
